<title>UK: Rentokil says to appeal against Clark ruling.</title>
<headline>Rentokil says to appeal against Clark ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Services group Rentokil Initial Plc said on Wednesday that it will appeal against a High Court ruling which awarded damages of more than three million stg to former BET Plc chief executive John Clark.  </p>
<p>Clark alleged that Rentokil had wrongfully dismissed him after its hostile takeover of BET Plc earlier this year.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Rentokil Initial said the damages awarded were &quot;an absolutely enormous sum of money, and clearly we are going to appeal.&quot;</p>
<p>The spokesman said its original offer to Clark following his dismissal was in line with those accepted &quot;by all other BET executives.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
